Krita Nova 49 - no safe assert in addDerivedResourceConverter (Ctrl+Shift+N)

"Paste into New Image" (Ctrl+Shift+N) and other ways of opening a second
canvas showed SAFE ASSERT "!m_derivedResources.contains(converter->key())"
(KoResourceManager_p.cpp; upstream bug 511060). The canvas resource manager
is shared by all the canvases of a window, and KoToolManager registers the
active tool's derived-resource converters (e.g. the opacity converter) on it:
the new canvas' tool registered a key that the other canvas' tool had
registered already.

- connectActiveTool(): a converter already registered for the key is
  replaced by the active tool's.
- disconnectActiveTool(): a tool removes a key only if the registered
  converter is still its own (another canvas' tool may have replaced it).
- KoResourceManager / KoCanvasResourceProvider::derivedResourceConverter(key).
